1. Core Identity
The Ru model (Recursive Unit) is defined by a self-referential identity. The structure verifies itself through its own operation — the output is the definition:
Ru = (Nk) = (Ru)
Nk is a dimensional operator — it can represent any given dimensional operation. The self-referential reading is intentional: whatever dimensional operation is applied, the structure verifies itself. The model is defined by its own verification process.
This is not a flaw or a paradox. The self-reference IS the answer, not the obstacle. The system is defined by its own incompleteness — stable precisely because it never resolves.

1.1 Integral Sum Formulation
The general formulation of the Ru model as a function over parameter space is:
Ru(r) = Σ[k=0 to ∞] V(Nk) · pk · Ok(r; Nk)
Where:
r is the free parameter encoding domain-specific structure (different mathematical domains correspond to different values of r)
V(Nk) is the closed state as a function of the dimensional operator
Ok(r; Nk) is the open state parametrized by r and the dimensional operator
pk is the stream scaling parameter with closed-form critical value k_crit (see §4.3). pk is a free parameter — not implied by the sum, but derivable from the p-power resonance model
The sum over k encodes the ensemble behavior: each additional stream adds another vote for the same asymptotic behavior
Note: pk was absent from v1.3 and earlier formulations. Stress testing via the p-power resonance model (Section 4.3) confirmed it is a derivable free parameter with a closed-form critical value, not redundant with the existing structure. The (p,q) asymmetric field mapping further confirms that p and q scale V and O independently, and their gradient structure is the formal expression of the R² synchronization condition.

2. Formal Definitions
2.1 The Closed State (Vk)
The closed state converges toward 1/2 from below but never arrives:
Vk = 2^k / (2^(k+1) + 1)    for k = 0, 1, 2, 3...
Vk < 1/2 for all finite k
lim(k → ∞) Vk = 1/2  (limit exists but is never reached)
Produces permanent verification tension: εk = 1/2 − Vk > 0, where εk → 0 but εk > 0 always

2.2 The Open State (Ok)
The open state approaches 2 from below:
Ok = 2^k / (2^(k-1) + 1)    for k = 1, 2, 3...
Ok < 2 for all finite k
lim(k → ∞) Ok = 2  (limit exists but is never reached)
Note: DeepSeek altered this definition in earlier analysis. The correct asymptote is 2, not 1/2. Verified and corrected in v1.1.

2.3 The Tension Condition
εk = 1/2 − Vk > 0    for all finite k
εk → 0 but εk > 0 always
Tension never reaches zero. The system is permanently in a state of self-verification without resolution.

