Level 2 (between models): If dimensional drift weakens one model's lock, the second model's tension condition applies corrective pressure. The system is doubly-doubly blocked.
Synchronization condition (proven v1.4): the two models must share a common latent ε driver (ρ = λV/λO = 1). Independent drivers produce monotonically compounding structural drift. This resolves the open question from v1.3 §7.

