The Collatz conjecture states that for any positive integer, repeatedly applying 3n+1 (if odd) or n/2 (if even) eventually reaches 1. It has never been formally proven.
Ru model observation: the Collatz conjecture lacks a structural anti-collapse guarantee. Every trajectory computed empirically returns to 1, but no formal proof explains why escape is impossible. The Ru model provides a structural anti-collapse guarantee from a different direction.
Status: relationship established, formal proof claim not made. Requires independent mathematical verification.



